 "notes": [
  "Official sites could not be read: textbooksonline.tn.nic.in (robots disallowed for the fetch tool; shell has no internet), tnschools.gov.in/scert e-books page (JavaScript-rendered, no content returned), textbookcorp.tn.gov.in price-list PDF (robots disallowed), dge.tn.gov.in (no syllabus/blueprint notices visible). Textbook content was therefore read from copies of the official TNTBESC/SCERT PDF hosted on cdn1.byjus.com; the front matter (Government of Tamil Nadu, SCERT copyright) identifies it as the official book. Chapters are marked verified:true on that basis.",
  "Term structure: the 2018 First Edition was printed in trimester pattern (Term I: Set Language, Real Numbers, Algebra, Geometry, Coordinate Geometry; Term II: Set Language, Real Numbers, Algebra, Geometry, Statistics; Term III: Algebra, Coordinate Geometry, Trigonometry, Mensuration, Probability). The 2019 Revised Edition is a single volume with nine chapters, and this file follows it (terms:null, term:null on all chapters). TNTBESC 2026-27 notices list term-wise books only for Std 1-7, which supports single-volume Std 9; not confirmed by an explicit Std 9 notice.",
  "Edition for 2026-27: News (DT Next, 16 Sep 2026) says the new State Education Policy syllabus applies in 2026-27 only to classes 1-3, with remaining classes from the next academic year, so Std 9 should still use the Revised Edition 2019 content (annual reprint; a '2025 Edition' file circulates). Some third-party sites (tnkalvi.net, tntextbooks.in) label the Std 9 Maths file 'new syllabus 2026-27'; I could not open that file to check whether its content differs. If TN issued a revised Std 9 Maths book for 2026-27, this file must be re-checked.",
  "Reduced syllabus: Covid-era reductions (2020-21 to 2022-23) were withdrawn and full syllabus restored from the 2023 exams (secondary news). Std 9 has no public exam, and no 2026-27 reduction notice was found. A third-party 'month-wise syllabus 2026-27' (padasalai.net) exists but its maths file was labelled 2025-26 and was not opened.",
  "Section lists contain only the numbered top-level sections from the official contents page (x.y). Sub-sections (e.g. 3.6.2 Synthetic Division, 3.8.1 Simultaneous Linear Equations, 4.7.1-4.7.4 triangle-centre constructions, 8.5.2 grouped median) were seen in chapter PDFs and are reflected in outcomes but not listed as sections.",
  "Chapter 3 section 3.8 (Linear Equation in Two Variables) covers simultaneous equations by graphical, substitution, elimination and cross-multiplication methods plus consistency. Consistency was taught through examples, not a separately numbered heading in the copy read.",
  "Chapter 8 (Statistics) covers grouped median and grouped mode as well as grouped mean (direct, assumed-mean, step-deviation), which goes beyond NCERT Class 9; these are mapped to MATH.statistics.grouped-mean (Grade 10 in the list).",
  "Trigonometric-table lookup (6.4) has no matching competency; mapped partially to MATH.trigonometry.ratios rather than proposing a lookup-only competency.",
  "Synthetic division is mapped to existing polynomial/factor-theorem competencies (it is a method, not a separate skill). Polynomial GCD is a proposed competency, shared with Grade 10.",
  "MATH.algebra.sets is listed as Grade 11 and MATH.trigonometry.ratios / MATH.coordinate.distance / MATH.algebra.linear-systems as Grade 10 in competencies-v1; TN teaches these in Grade 9. The mapping is by skill, not grade."
 ],
